<section xml:id="aboutcsp">

  <title>About AP CSP</title>

  <p>
  AP Computer Science Principles (CSP) is an introductory college-level computing course 
  designed to introduce students to the field of computer science, Artificial Intelligence (AI), and its applications.
  Rather than focusing only on coding, AP CSP explores the broader ideas of computing,
  including Artificial Intelligence (AI), data, the Internet, cybersecurity, 
  and the impacts of computing on society. No prior programming experience is required.
  Find out more about the AP exam at <url href="https://apcentral.collegeboard.org/courses/ap-computer-science-principles">
  College Board AP CSP site</url>. </p>
  
  <p>CSPossible was created for the new 2027-2028 
    <url href="https://apcentral.collegeboard.org/courses/ap-computer-science-principles/redesign">College Board AP CSP redesign.</url>
    It follows the learning objectives and essential knowledge outlined in the <url href="https://apcentral.collegeboard.org/media/pdf/ap-computer-science-principles-course-framework-effective-fall-2027.pdf">
    new AP CSP Framework</url> for the 2027-2028 academic year. The AP Computer Science Principles course aligns with the core concepts in the 
    Computer Science Teachers Association (CSTA) K–12 Computer Science Framework. 
  </p>

  <p>The new 2027-2028 AP CSP framework is organized into 4 units that incorporate using AI responsibly and 
    text-based programming in languages such as Python. 
  </p>
   <ol>
    <li>Unit 1: Creating Purposeful Apps and Programs </li>
    <li>Unit 2: Building Solutions using Selection and Iteration</li>
    <li>Unit 3: Abstraction using Lists and Procedures</li>
    <li>Unit 4: Data-Driven Decisions using the Internet and AI</li>
  </ol>
  
  <p>The new AP CSP framework will also include a new AI Create Project, in which students build an AI application. 
    More information about this project will be released in Spring 2027. The AP Exam will include free-response 
    questions about the project, similar to previous years. New AI labs aligned to the course framework will be 
    available through AP Classroom.
  </p>

 </section>